questions.answer:
A line graph with:
- **independent variable on the $x$-axis:** "Duration of diabetes (years)", with an even scale from 0 to 35;
- **dependent variable on the $y$-axis:** "Percentage of participants with glaucoma (%)", with an even scale from 0 to 14;
- all eight points plotted accurately (as crosses);
- a single smooth curve (or line) of best fit — not dot-to-dot;
- a title, e.g. "Percentage of diabetic participants with glaucoma vs duration of diabetes".
